#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# asymptotic_less_equal

#% text
# `asymptotic_less_equal(f, g, x -> a)` gives true when f = O(g) as x approaches a: |f/g| stays bounded near a.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Decided by `max_limit(abs(f/g), x -> a)`: a finite value gives true, inf gives false; an undecided limit gives `failure(undecided, ...)`.

#% item
# Options: `direction:` as for `limit` (from_above, from_below, two_sided, -1, 1, ...); `assumptions:` facts on the parameters.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
asymptotic_less_equal(x, x^2, x -> inf)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
asymptotic_less_equal(1/x^2, 1/(x*sin(x)), x -> 0)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
asymptotic_less_equal(sin(x), x*unit_step(x), x -> 0, direction: from_above)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
asymptotic_less_equal(x^2, x, x -> inf)
#% output
#= false

